  "rai:dataCollection": "Hand-authored by the dataset author. Each functional reference specifies a canonical MLIR function name, signature, concrete inputs, and the expected scalar/array output under the dialect's execution wrapper (mlir-cpu-runner for arith and linalg+memref; iree-run-module for StableHLO).",
  "rai:dataBiases": [
    "Author-curated: prompts reflect the dataset author's mental model of the target dialect; the 10-per-dialect sample biases toward elementary numerical operations.",
    "No human-subject data; no PII; no demographic bias dimensions apply."
  ],
  "rai:dataLimitations": [
    "Functional correctness is checked via stdout pattern matching and scalar/array equality on a small set of fixed inputs; this is a coarser signal than property-based or random-input testing.",
    "Each task has exactly one reference implementation; alternate valid implementations may diverge on edge cases.",
    "n=30 is a regression-style spot check, not a comprehensive functional benchmark."
  ],
  "rai:annotationsPerExample": 0,
  "rai:annotationDemographics": "N/A — no human annotators.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "None.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": [
    "Spot-checking that verify-valid generations on the sibling Spec-30/Spec-150 benchmarks compute the intended function.",
    "Reporting a verify-vs-functional gap on a hand-authored sample.",
    "Out of scope: comprehensive functional benchmark suitable as the sole metric for ranking systems — size and coverage are insufficient; training or fine-tuning production code-generation models."
  ],
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "This benchmark is intended to spot-check functional correctness of MLIR generations evaluated against verifier-only metrics. It contains no human-subject, demographic, or PII content, and poses no direct risk to individuals or groups. The principal social risk is methodological: at n=30, results are a regression-style spot check, not a deployment-readiness signal — over-reliance on this set could lead to overstated claims about model capability. Pair with property-based or random-input testing before drawing conclusions.",
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": false,
